Version 0.3-0

  *   Works with current R (tested on R 4.6.1). The package now has its own
      XML-RPC client built on curl and xml2 and no longer needs the XMLRPC
      package (never on CRAN), RCurl or XML. Everything installs from CRAN.

  *   Calls are now valid XML-RPC: structs and arrays are wrapped in <value>,
      times keep their minutes (XMLRPC wrote %H:%H:%S), doubles are written
      without exponents, factors are sent as strings, and NA/Inf raise an error
      instead of being sent as text.

  *   Responses: empty arrays no longer error, <nil/>, <i8> and dates with
      dashes or time zones are handled, and a BOM/whitespace before the XML
      declaration is tolerated. HTTP errors (e.g. XML-RPC disabled by the
      host) report the status and message instead of "Problems".

  *   guessMIMEType() is vectorized (it failed in R >= 4.2), works without
      attaching the package, and falls back to application/octet-stream.

  *   newPost()/editPost()/newPage(): a single category is sent as an array
      (WordPress ignored it otherwise, e.g. from knitr::knit2wp()),
      mt_keywords may be a character vector, and multi-element descriptions
      are collapsed into one string.

  *   newCategory() sends the struct WordPress expects; it previously created
      a category named after the first letter only.

  *   getPostStatusList() called wp.getPageStatusList.

  *   setPostCategories() sends an array (not a struct) of categories, accepts
      numeric ids, and deleteCategory()/matchCategory() return ids rather than
      names for fuzzy matches.

  *   uploadFile() supports in-memory content via I() or raw vectors.

  *   getPosts()/getPages() handle empty results and fields missing from some
      posts.

  *   appendToPost() works and is exported, as is guessMIMEType().

  *   Added a test suite, including a fake WordPress XML-RPC server.

Version 0.2-3

  *   Another fix for editPost() found by Daniel Wollschlaeger.
      content can be a list() with fields describing the structure
      or a simple character string.

Version 0.2-2

  *   Fix for editPost() to not include the appId
      Found by Daniel Wollschlaeger.

Version 0.2-1

  *   Fix of type for uploadFile() in computing the default value for the MIME type.

Version 0.2-0

  *   Allow the user to specify the location of the server URL.